@@ c-comment
@@ c-intro
`modules/advent/` is a self-contained, transferable Advent calendar (spec `docs/specs/advent-calendar.md`, plan `docs/advent/build-plan.md`, details `modules/advent/README.md`). It is **live**: the page `/advent` shows the real calendar from 1 December (door grid, day dialog, gentle "Not quite yet" card, share, print, archive until 6 January, the 6 January bonus door) and the home page shows a banner while it is open; before and after the season the page shows only the calm sentence "The Advent calendar opens on 1 December.". The page is in the sitemap and the site search (one result), but in no nav or footer link. `?advent-preview=2026-12-07` still shows any date while `previewEnabled` is true.
@@ c-launch
- **Launched** (date of the launch commit: ____). The three launch flags in `theme.mjs` (`goLive`, `publicListing`, `artRequired`) are all `true`, and the three pre-launch guard tests are gone. `VERSION`/`MANIFEST.sha256` pin the generic code: after changing it run `npm run advent:manifest` and bump `VERSION`. Fixture themes in the unit tests pin the three flags to false (`test-unit/support/fixture-flags.mjs`); keep it that way. `npm run advent:rehearse` still copies the repo and runs the unit suite with the flags flipped, which is the quick check that a change has not broken the launched state.
@@ c-flags
- **Launch flags in `theme.mjs`:** `goLive` (the real date drives the calendar and the home banner), `publicListing` (in the sitemap and search, no noindex) and `artRequired` (the build refuses a missing `public/advent/art/day-NN.svg`) are `true`; the schema refuses `goLive` without the other two. `previewEnabled` decides whether `?advent-preview=` still works: security recommends setting it to `false` after 6 January. No flag adds a nav, footer or home-page link. The browser tests force `goLive` on through `forceGoLive` (`test/support/advent.ts`).
@@ c-home
- **Home page:** `src/pages/index.html` has `{{ADVENT_TEASER}}` INSIDE the hero section (so the home page is laid out identically outside the season): one empty hidden container and two script tags (the tiny classic `advent-early.js`, which, only when the banner is about to show, moves the container after the hero and reserves its height in rem BEFORE the first paint so the banner does not push the page down, and the banner module `advent-teaser.js`, which releases the reservation), no text, link or heading in the source; the banner script builds the banner and shows it only inside the season. `test-unit/advent-built.test.mjs` documents exactly what the home page may contain, and `test-unit/advent-early.test.mjs` runs the early script against the real date rules for every day. Never add calendar text or a link to the home page source.
@@ c-help
- The help guide `src/pages/help-advent.html` (plain English: previewing, editing a day, replacing a picture, after the season) is now listed in the help search scope and may mention the calendar; no other page may mention `advent-preview`, besides the unlinked `/updates`.
